Now index.js.

Careful with texture disposal: track `this.ownedTextures = []`.

The sky material is shared between the sky dome and PMREM temp scene; `makeEnvironment` disposes the temp sphere geometry only. The env target textures must be disposed on unload.

Number textures: `texNumber` returns a texture; track.

Wheel face textures: in `this.textures` (shared, not disposed).

On unload: dispose envDry/envWet, traverse scene for geometries/materials, dispose owned number textures. Don't dispose shared textures.

Watch out: the sky material is in `this.scene` via the mesh; disposing the material is fine. It's not reused across loads.

`this.scene.environment` = env render target texture; dispose target after clearing.

Let me write.

Constructor:
```js
export class Race3D {
  constructor(canvas){
    this.canvas=canvas;
    this.renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({canvas, antialias:true, powerPreference:'high-performance'});
    ...
    this.textures = {...}
    this.resize();
  }
```
Note `texCarbon` returns a texture with repeat 2,2; fine.

In `load`:
```js
this.unload();
this.game=game;
this.style=CAR_STYLES[clamp(game.eraIndex,0,8)];
this.textures... 
this.layout=buildLayout(game.track, game.eraIndex);
this.sunDir=new THREE.Vector3();
const az=2.35, el=0.36; // elevation ~21deg
this.sunDir.set(Math.cos(el)*Math.cos(az), Math.sin(el), Math.cos(el)*Math.sin(az)).normalize();
this.scene=new THREE.Scene();
this.scene.fog=new THREE.Fog(0xccd7da, 180, 1500);
this.sky=createSkyDome(this.sunDir,'DRY');
this.scene.add(this.sky.mesh);
setSkyWeather(this.sky,'DRY');
this.envDry=makeEnvironment(this.renderer,this.sky);
setSkyWeather(this.sky,'WET');
this.envWet=makeEnvironment(this.renderer,this.sky);
setSkyWeather(this.sky,'DRY');
this.buildLighting();
this.buildWorld(game);
this.weather=null;
this.applyWeather(game.weather||'DRY');
this.camInit=false;
this.station=-1;
this.time=0;
this.prevSpeed=game.player.speed;
```

Hmm `makeEnvironment` uses the same renderer while the scene may exist. Fine.

The env map orientation: PMREM from a scene with a sphere at origin; the sky sphere's material is BackSide, camera at origin inside. Good.

`buildLighting`:
```js
this.sun=new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xfff2d9, 3.1);
this.sun.castShadow=true;
const size = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio||1,2) > 1.5 ? 2048 : 1536;
this.sun.shadow.mapSize.set(size,size);
this.sun.shadow.camera.left=-42; right=42; top=42; bottom=-42; near=1; far=340;
this.sun.shadow.bias=-0.0006; this.sun.shadow.normalBias=0.06;
this.scene.add(this.sun, this.sun.target);
this.hemi=new THREE.HemisphereLight(0xbcd6ee,0x46503f,.75);
this.scene.add(this.hemi);
```
Directional light position will be updated each frame relative to the player.

`buildWorld`:
```js
const road=buildRoad(this.layout,this.textures); this.road=road; this.scene.add(road.group);
const terrain=buildTerrain(this.layout,this.textures); this.scene.add(terrain.mesh);
this.scene.add(buildTrees(this.layout).group);
const sc=buildScenery(this.layout,this.game.track,this.game.eraIndex,this.textures);
this.scene.add(sc.group); this.startLightMat=sc.startLightMat;
this.shared={carbon:this.textures.carbon, wheelFaceVintage:..., wheelFaceModern:...};
...
this.sunFlare=makeSunFlare(); this.scene.add(this.sunFlare);
this.rain=makeRain(); this.scene.add(this.rain);
```

Wait `makeRain`'s material opacity 0 and visible false; applyWeather sets.

Also add a low "grass" fog? no.

Stations:
```js
this.stations=Array.from({length:14},(_,i)=>{const u=i/14+.006; const sm=this.layout.sample(u); const s=i%2?1:-1; const p=sm.pos.clone().addScaledVector(sm.side,s*(this.layout.halfWidth+13)); p.y+=4.4+(i%3)*1.4; return {u,pos:p};});
```

Number textures: `this.ownedTextures=[]; const num = texNumber(1,'#f2f2e8'); this.ownedTextures.push(num);`

Player accent: era.colors[1] might be very dark or light; fine.

Helmet color: era.colors[1] or white. Use '#eceae0' for player with accent stripe? Keep white.

AI accent: lum>.62 ? '#141618' : '#f0f0e6'.

Also the player's number texture color should contrast; use '#f2f2e8'.

`applyWeather` sets `this.scene.environment`. Sky mesh follows camera in render.

Now `unload`:
```js
unload(){
  if(this.envDry) {this.envDry.dispose(); this.envDry=null;}
  ...
  if(this.scene){
    this.scene.traverse(o=>{
      if(o.geometry) o.geometry.dispose();
      if(o.material){
        const mats=Array.isArray(o.material)?o.material:[o.material];
        for(const m of mats){ if(m.map && m.map.userData?.owned) m.map.dispose(); m.dispose(); }
      }
    });
    this.scene.clear?.();
    this.scene.environment=null;
  }
  (this.ownedTextures||[]).forEach(t=>t.dispose());
  this.ownedTextures=[];
  ...
}
```
Textures referenced in materials (asphalt, grass, kerb, etc.) shouldn't be disposed by material.dispose (they aren't). Only owned number textures disposed separately. But `texNumber` textures are also used as material.map and disposed separately — fine, disposing twice is okay? Texture.dispose twice triggers events twice; harmless.

But wait, `this.scene.traverse` will also hit the sky mesh's ShaderMaterial (no map) and dispose. Fine. However PMREM env targets are not in the scene.

`this.scene.clear()` exists in r160? Scene.clear() added? Object3D.clear() exists. Fine.

After unload, set this.scene = null.

Renderer info memory: fine.

`render` must guard `if(!this.ready) return`.

Also `this.renderer.render` gets called when the panel is hidden? frame loop stops when leaving.

Now camera update. Need to handle `game.camera` modes and helmet visibility.

For chase, the camera world position smoothing should not go through the terrain; the camera at ~2.6m above the track; on elevation changes, okay. If the camera lags on corners it may cut a corner; acceptable.

Add camera shake:
```js
const shake = (this.wet?0.02:0.01)*speedRatio;
this.camera.position.x += Math.sin(this.time*47.3)*shake;
this.camera.position.y += Math.cos(this.time*39.7)*shake*.7;
```

Look at:
```js
this.camera.lookAt(this.camLook);
```

Cockpit: hide helmet. Note the cockpit camera sees the halo and front wing. Set FOV 72? F1 onboard ~70-90. Use 74. Position local (0, .97, .18), look (0,.92,30). Since it's inside the body near the halo, near plane .07 may clip the halo bar but it's at .81-.95 around z ±.3; camera at z=.18, y=.97; the halo bar at z=-.02..-.52 and y=.95: behind the camera mostly. Front pillar at z=cockpitZ+.46≈1.2, y=.88; visible. Good.

Actually camera at z=cockpitZ+.18=~1.0; the nose is ahead; fine. Put camera at y=.99 (above the halo hoop) for a clear view. Halo top at .95; camera .99 just above. F1 onboard cameras are mounted above the halo. Good.

TV: station positions fixed; lookAt smoothed? Just lookAt car. Add FOV based on distance to car: `const d=station.pos.distanceTo(pose.pos); fov=clamp(46 - d*0.55, 22, 46)`. With d ~ 20m → 35. That's telephoto; good broadcast feel. Camera should maybe pan smoothly; the car moves smoothly so fine.

Heli: smooth camPos.

Sun flare: `this.sunFlare.position.copy(this.camera.position).addScaledVector(this.sunDir, 900)`; sprite scale 260. Check if the sun is behind the camera: flare will render at the sun's screen position even if off-screen (sprite clipped). Fine. But with depthTest false it may show through the ground if the sun is below the horizon — sun elevation 21° so no.

Rain: `this.rain.position.copy(this.camera.position)`. Update y positions each frame (only when visible).

Rain velocity: local y -= dt*55; if y < 0 → y += 55.

Dust: skip (time).

Also wheel spray in wet: skip.

Start lights: `this.startLightMat.emissiveIntensity = game.started ? 0 : (game.lights>0 ? 5 : 0)`. But countdown lights: the game's `lights` increments 1..5 then at start hides. Good. Maybe add a green light? skip.

Brake light: get braking from game keys? `keys` is global in game.js, not accessible here. We can pass via `game.braking` — not set. Use speed decrease: `this.prevSpeed - p.speed > 0.5` → braking. Set emissiveIntensity 4 else 1.2.

Also headlights for wet? no.

Render:
```js
render(game, dt){
 if(!this.ready) return;
 this.time += dt;
 this.applyWeatherIfNeeded(game);
 this.updateCars(game, dt);
 this.updateCamera(game, dt);
 this.updateSunAndSky(game);
 this.updateEffects(game, dt);
 this.updateLights(game);
 this.renderer.render(this.scene, this.camera);
}
```

Resize: `this.resize()` called after load too since the canvas may have changed.

Note: The first load may occur while `#raceScreen` is visible (display fixed). Good.

Now the `orientCar` uses `layout.sample` which allocates. Also the camera needs the player pose. Fine.

`updateCars`:
```js
const p=game.player;
const accel=(p.speed-this.prevSpeed)/Math.max(dt,.001);
this.prevSpeed=p.speed;
const pose=orientCar(this.playerRig,this.layout,p.distance,p.lateral*this.layout.halfWidth,dt,p.speed,p.steer,{player:true,pitch:clamp(-accel*.0009,-.022,.022), yawOffset:p.steer*.05});
this.playerPose=pose;
game.ai.forEach((ai,i)=>{
  const rig=this.aiRigs[i]; if(!rig) return;
  const steer=Math.sin(this.time*.7+i*2.1)*.18;
  orientCar(rig,this.layout,ai.distance,ai.lateral*this.layout.halfWidth*.82,dt,ai.speed,steer,{});
});
```

Note player lateral meters = lateral * halfWidth (as reasoned). Good.

AI cars start behind, some may be >1 lap apart; u handles.

`this.playerRig.root.updateMatrixWorld(true)` before cockpit localToWorld.

Cockpit localToWorld with root works? `root.localToWorld(vec)` uses matrixWorld, updated in render by the renderer, but we're before rendering; call `updateMatrixWorld(true)`.

`updateCamera`:
```js
const pose=this.playerPose;
const p=this.game.player;
const ratio=clamp(p.speed/this.game.era.max,0,1);
const mode=this.game.camera|0;
this.playerRig.helmet.visible = mode!==1;
...
```
When switching modes, snap or smooth? Keep `this.camInit`; when mode changes, snap (`this.camMode!==mode` → init false). Set `this.camMode=mode`.

