content.text:
Now start line rotation fix in layout.js:

```js
const line = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(half*2,1.7), mat);
line.rotation.x=-Math.PI/2; line.rotation.y=yaw;
```
Replace geometry with pre-rotated:
```js
const lineGeo = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(half*2, 1.7);
lineGeo.rotateX(-Math.PI/2);
const line = new THREE.Mesh(lineGeo, mat);
line.rotation.y = yaw;
```
But local X of the plane after rotateX lies along X; we need it along the side vector. Since side = right and tangent determines yaw, with yaw aligning local +Z to tangent, local X = ... rotation.y=yaw maps local X to (cos yaw,0,-sin yaw). For tangent=(sin yaw,0,cos yaw), local X = (cos yaw,0,-sin yaw) which is perpendicular = -side? side = (-t.z,0,t.x) = (-cos yaw,0,sin yaw) = -localX. So local X is opposite side, but that's fine for a symmetric line.

Also the start line's position y + .12 → floats 12cm above the road (road crown at 0.045 max). Lower to +.06.

Let me patch.

